    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32760" root="غيق" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَاقٌ</span></b>  <i>A certain aquatic bird;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَاقَةٌ</span></b> .
(Lth, O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And The <i>crow,</i> or <i>raven:</i>
(ISd, K:) so sometimes called because of his
cry. (ISd, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَاقِ</span> is a word imitative of
<i>The cry</i> [i. e. <i>caw</i>] of the crow, or raven: when
indeterminate, [meaning <i>a caw,</i>] it is with tenween, (IJ, S, O, K,) i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَاقٍ</span>. (IJ, TA.)

